 *
 * ## Overview
 *
 * PicoKernel welcomes contributors of all experience levels. These expectations
 * exist to keep the project healthy, sustainable, and welcoming for everyone.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Licensing
 *
 * PicoKernel source code is licensed under **GPL-3.0-or-later**.
 *
 * | Requirement | Detail |
 * |-------------|--------|
 * | License compatibility | All contributed code must be compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later |
 * | SPDX header | Every `.c`, `.h`, and `.dox` file must carry relevant SPDX block |
 * | No proprietary code | Do not submit code you do not have the right to contribute |
 * | No license contamination | Do not introduce dependencies with incompatible licenses |
 * | DCO | By opening a PR, you confirm the contribution is your own work or appropriately licensed |
 *
 * By opening a Pull Request, you confirm:
 * > *"I have the right to submit this contribution, and I agree it will be
 * > distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later."*
 *
 * See [LICENSE](https://codeberg.org/PicoKernel/PicoKernel/src/branch/main/LICENSES/).
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Testing Expectations
 *
 * | Requirement | Enforcement |
 * |-------------|-------------|
 * | Code compiles cleanly without warnings | **Required**, PR will not merge otherwise |
 * | Bug fixes include a description of how the fix was verified | **Required** |
 * | Test output included in PR description | **Required** where applicable |
 * | Edge cases considered and documented | Strongly recommended |
 *
 * PicoKernel does not yet have a formal automated test framework. Until one
 * is established, test evidence means:
 * - Build output confirming clean compilation
 * - UART/USB output demonstrating correct runtime behaviour
 * - Manual description of what was exercised and what was observed
 *
 * @note When a test framework is established, this section will be updated
 * and automated test requirements will be enforced at review.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Documentation Expectations
 *
 * | Requirement | Enforcement |
 * |-------------|-------------|
 * | All public APIs documented with Doxygen | **Blocked** without it |
 * | SPDX + file header on every modified file | **Blocked** without it |
 * | `.dox` pages updated if behaviour changes | **Required** |
 * | Diagrams updated if architecture changes | **Required** |
 *
 * Full documentation standards: @ref docs_style.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Code Ownership
 *
 * | Principle | Detail |
 * |-----------|--------|
 * | Collective ownership | No contributor owns a subsystem exclusively |
 * | Reviewers may request changes from anyone | - |
 * | Maintainers have final merge authority | Final decisions rest with project maintainers |
 * | Refactoring is welcome | Improvement PRs are encouraged, raise an issue first for large changes |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Review Conduct
 *
 * Code review is a technical conversation, not a judgment of the contributor.
 *
 * | Expectation | For contributors | For reviewers |
 * |-------------|-----------------|---------------|
 * | Be specific | Address all feedback before merge | Comment on the code, not the person |
 * | Disagree constructively | Push back with reasoning | Explain the why behind every request |
 * | Respond promptly | Don't leave PRs idle for weeks | Don't leave reviews pending for weeks |
 * | Close cleanly | Update or close stale PRs | Request changes clearly |
 *
 * @note A requested change you disagree with is an invitation to a technical
 * discussion not a rejection. Raise your reasoning in the PR comments.
 * The best outcome is always understanding, not compliance.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Communication
 *
 * | Channel | Purpose |
 * |---------|---------|
 * | [Codeberg Issues](https://codeberg.org/PicoKernel/PicoKernel/issues) | Bug reports, feature requests, design proposals |
 * | Pull Request comments | Code-level discussion |
 * | Issue comments | Design and planning discussion |
 * | [Discord](https://discord.gg/Ucb9xt8B6r) | For general stuff | 
 *
 * For significant architectural changes, open an issue for discussion before
 * writing code. A PR that changes architecture without prior discussion is
 * likely to be returned for redesign.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Summary Checklist
 *
 * Before opening any Pull Request:
 *
 * - [ ] Contribution is GPL-3.0-or-later compatible
 * - [ ] SPDX block present on all new or modified files
 * - [ ] All public APIs have complete Doxygen documentation
 * - [ ] Code compiles cleanly: `cmake --build build`
 * - [ ] Test evidence included in the PR description
 * - [ ] Branch targets `dev`, not `main`
 * - [ ] PR title, summary, and test evidence fields are filled
 * - [ ] No architecture violations
 * - [ ] No debug output outside `#ifdef KERNEL_DEBUG`
 *
